    "['esqm service-stream [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip flow monitor YOUR-FLOW-MONITOR-NAME input', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Based on the Huawei configuration context, `esqm service-stream inbound` appears to be enabling Enhanced Stream Quality Monitoring (ESQM) for inbound service streams on the interface. The closest Cisco equivalent would be enabling NetFlow or Flexible NetFlow for traffic monitoring on an interface.\\n\\nFor Cisco devices, the equivalent would typically be:\\n##\\nip flow monitor YOUR-FLOW-MONITOR-NAME input\\n##\\n\\nNote: You would need to define the flow monitor separately in Cisco's configuration. The exact implementation may vary depending on your monitoring requirements and Cisco platform.\\n\\nIf you're specifically looking for QoS monitoring, an alternative might be:\\n##\\nservice-policy input YOUR-POLICY-NAME\\n##\\n\\nWhere YOUR-POLICY-NAME would be a predefined QoS policy.\", 'trans_template': 'ip flow monitor YOUR-FLOW-MONITOR-NAME input'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'service-policy input YOUR-POLICY-NAME', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Based on the Huawei configuration context, `esqm service-stream inbound` appears to be enabling Enhanced Stream Quality Monitoring (ESQM) for inbound service streams on the interface. The closest Cisco equivalent would be enabling NetFlow or Flexible NetFlow for traffic monitoring on an interface.\\n\\nFor Cisco devices, the equivalent would typically be:\\n##\\nip flow monitor YOUR-FLOW-MONITOR-NAME input\\n##\\n\\nNote: You would need to define the flow monitor separately in Cisco's configuration. The exact implementation may vary depending on your monitoring requirements and Cisco platform.\\n\\nIf you're specifically looking for QoS monitoring, an alternative might be:\\n##\\nservice-polic