    "['[parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip flow-export version 9', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ip flow-export version 9', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'The `esqm` command in Huawei devices stands for \"Enhanced Stream Quality Monitoring,\" which is a feature for monitoring service traffic quality. In Cisco devices, the equivalent functionality would typically be implemented using IP SLA (Service Level Agreement) or NetFlow for traffic monitoring and analysis.\\n\\nHowever, since `esqm` appears as a standalone command in the global configuration (without specific parameters), the closest Cisco equivalent would be enabling NetFlow or IP SLA globally. \\n\\nFor a direct translation (though not feature-exact), the closest would be enabling NetFlow:\\n\\n##\\nip flow-export version 9\\nip flow-export destination <collector-ip> <port>\\n##\\n\\nNote: There isn\\'t a perfect 1:1 mapping since `esqm` is Huawei-specific. The above assumes basic traffic monitoring functionality. For exact feature parity, additional context about the `esqm` implementation would be needed.', 'trans_template': 'ip flow-export version 9'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip flow-export destination <collector-ip> <port>', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ip flow-export destination <collector-ip> <port>', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'The `esqm` command in Huawei devices stands for \"Enhanced Stream Quality Monitoring,\" which is a feature for monitoring service traffic quality. In Cisco devices, the equivalent functionality would typically be implemented using IP SLA (Service Level Agreement) or NetFlow for traffic monitoring and analysis.\\n\\nHowever, since `esqm` appears as a standalone command in the global configuration (without specific parameters), the closest Cisco equivalent would be enabling NetFlow or IP SLA globally. \\n\\nFor a direct translation (though not feature-exact), the closest would be enabling NetFlow:\\n\\n##\\nip flow-export version 9\\nip